def report(run):
 verify(run,'readout_lock.json');summary=read(run/'latent_metric_summary.json');models0=read(run/'selected_models.json');man=read(run/'context_manifest.json');jm=read(run/'jacobian_checks.json');outputrows=csvread(run/'output_metrics.csv');response=csvread(run/'finite_response_metrics.csv');fm=csvread(run/'all_feature_metrics.csv');diags=read(run/'solver_diagnostics.json');stability=csvread(run/'coefficient_stability.csv');predst=csvread(run/'prediction_stability.csv');primary=summary.get('primary_ordinary',{});rows=[]
 for method in ['native','input','output','semantic','shuffle','mean']:
  if method not in primary:continue
  r=primary[method];rows.append([method,models0[method]['alpha'],models0[method]['rank'],r['well_read'],format_value(r['median_NMSE']),format_value(r['p90_NMSE']),format_value(r['pooled_raw_MSE'])])
 selected=models0['native'];lines=['# Frozen latent correspondence v0.5','',f"Completed estimation of M (1024×256) and d (1024,) using frozen teacher and transcoder. Global alpha={selected['alpha']}; standardized native design rank={selected['rank']}/256; fit/selection counts11200/2800. No refit on their union. CUDA SVD and model identities passed; see process exit_status for completion. M is an estimated affine correspondence, not ground-truth D2, a unique hidden code or a causal pathway.",'',f"Exact artifacts: `{(run/'M.npy').resolve()}` and `{(run/'d.npy').resolve()}`; [readout checkpoint](readout.pt), [usage](HOW_TO_USE_M.md), [locked provenance](readout_lock.json). Predictions are raw `H@M.T+d`; negative predictions remain unmodified.",'','## 1. Numerical estimation and scope','',f"Fit-only eligible features={primary.get('native',{}).get('assessed_features','no primary support')}; fit-statistic details in fit_statistics.json. Rank cutoff rcond=1e-10; singular values, condition estimates, SVD reconstruction and normal-equation residuals saved for every control. The unregularized projection residual per feature is in native_solver.npz and measures finite-sample affine-span limitations, not optimization convergence. Dropped columns have zero final M; intercept is unpenalized. Teacher was accepted for this pilot despite failing its original all-primitive accuracy gate.",'',f"New primary ordinary inputs={len(man['ordinary_confirmation_keys'])}; unique primary inference union={len(man['primary_unique_keys'])}. Available density counts={man['sampling']['available_density']}; ordinary sample density={man['sampling']['ordinary_density']}. Every primary row excludes original dataset, final keys and recoverable historically scored keys. This is density-conditioned development evaluation, not IID generator sampling or final-population scoring. History may omit unrecorded exposure. Existing final-key index reused; reserved NPZ not opened.",'','## 2–3. Held-out latent readability and controls','',table(['predictor','alpha','design rank','well read /1024','median NMSE(fitvar)','p90 NMSE','pooled raw MSE'],rows),'', '“Well read” requires NMSE_fitvar≤0.05, meaningful-active relative RMSE≤0.20 and≥32 active rows. A dormant/rare/unsupported column is not called recovered from low zero-prediction MSE. R² uses each evaluation population’s own variance and may be undefined; it is distinct from1−NMSE_fitvar. All1024 feature rows, support counts, active/inactive/nearzero errors, negative predictions and controls are in [all-feature metrics](all_feature_metrics.csv). Fit, selection, ordinary primary, primary contexts and legacy are separate.','']
 if primary:
  best={}
  for method in ['input','output','semantic']:
   rr={r['feature']:r for r in fm if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']==method};native_rows=[r for r in fm if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']=='native'];best[method]=sum(float(r['mse'])<float(rr[r['feature']]['mse']) for r in native_rows)
  lines += [f'Native H has smaller ordinary-confirmation raw MSE than controls on this many of1024 features: {best}. Predictor dimensions differ, so superiority indicates predictive information under these affine models, not mechanistic equivalence. Mean and shuffled pairing controls bound trivial mean prediction and pairing dependence.','',f"Primary native unsupported features (<32 meaningful active)={primary['native']['unsupported_meaningful_lt32']}; newly activating={primary['native']['newly_activating']}; constant-evaluation columns={primary['native']['constant_eval']}; assessed variance-normalized features={primary['native']['assessed_features']}.",'']
 lines += ['## 4. Finite input changes and local derivatives','', 'No finite-change or derivative target entered regression or alpha selection. Four-corner values, baseline/single/joint coefficients, partner-off/on changes and nuisance changes are all evaluated using the same fixed M. Changes with |Δz|≥0.1·sqrt(fitvar) are the nontrivial subset; ratios use summed squared errors/target changes, not averages of unstable relative errors.','']
 rr=[]
 for pair in PAIRS:
  key=','.join(map(str,pair));bank=man['primary_contexts'][key];
  for typ in ['first_off','first_on','second_off','second_on','joint','nuisance']:
   rows0=[r for r in response if r['population']=='primary' and r['pair']==key and r['method']=='native' and r['change_type']==typ];relative=[float(r['nontrivial_relative_RMSE']) for r in rows0 if r['nontrivial_relative_RMSE']!=''];rr.append([key,bank['n_contexts'],len(bank['nuisance_edges']),typ,sum(r['finite_response_compatible']=='True' for r in rows0),float(np.median(relative)) if relative else 'undefined'])
 lines += [table(['pair','primary contexts','nuisance edges','change type','compatible /1024','median nontrivial relative RMSE'],rr),'',f"Jacobian sample={jm.get('n',0)} primary ordinary inputs; boundary inputs={jm.get('boundary_count','undefined')}; aggregate latent derivative relative Frobenius={jm.get('aggregate_relative_Frobenius','undefined')}. Both actual-x and P-column semantic-direction gradients are compared. P has rank12, so20 columns are not independent directions. Analytical derivatives were checked against autograd and finite differences only inside fixed-gate regions, with margins/steps retained. Boolean data do not supervise local continuous derivatives; disagreement does not directly imply Boolean failure.",'', 'Controls are evaluated on the same finite changes; see finite_response_metrics.csv. Primary support shortages are flagged rather than replaced by legacy results.','', '## 5. Output compatibility and cancellation','']
 oo=[]
 for method in ['native','input','output','semantic','shuffle','mean']:
  r=next((r for r in outputrows if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']==method and r['residual']=='teacher_minus_via'),None)
  if r:oo.append([method,r['full_MSE'],r['semantic_MSE'],r['out_of_Q_span_MSE']])
 floor=next((r for r in outputrows if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']=='native' and r['residual']=='teacher_minus_TC'),None);cancel=next((r for r in outputrows if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']=='native' and r['residual']=='latent_output_cancellation'),None)
 lines += [table(['latent predictor through frozen B','teacher residual12D MSE','semantic MSE','out-of-Q-span MSE'],oo),'',f'Full frozen TC error floor: {floor}. Native readout latent-error cancellation accounting: {cancel}. Individual feature error energy and summed decoder error are distinct; cancellation can hide latent failures.','', 'Verified identities: `F−(B zhat+c)=(F−T)+B(z−zhat)=(W2−BM)h+(b2−Bd−c)`. Parameter-map relative norms and data-weighted action error are in parameter_map_diagnostics.json; raw weight discrepancy in poorly observed hidden directions is not directly identifiable. Fixed feature-pair group contribution tests use the same M, with no group fitting or adaptive grouping. A good group sum never rescues failed individuals.','', '## 6. Stability and identifiability','']
 for half in ['half1','half2']:
  cs=[float(r['standardized_direction_cosine']) for r in stability if r['comparison']==half and r['standardized_direction_cosine']!=''];pp=[float(r[half+'_prediction_difference_RMSE']) for r in predst];lines += [f'{half}: median standardized coefficient direction cosine={np.median(cs) if cs else None}; median prediction difference RMSE versus primary={np.median(pp) if pp else None}. Half fits use the same selected global alpha, separate fit-only statistics, and never replace primary M.','']
 lines += ['Correlated hidden activations and finite data can give stable predictions with unstable coefficients. No uniqueness, invertibility, causal abstraction or sparse circuit claim follows. Dense readout readability is a different result from the v0.4 bounded-subset failures.','', '## 7. Six fixed computational examples','', 'Each report prints the complete TC equation, fitted M-weighted native equation, true original biases, fit-only contribution panel, numeric four-corner gates, signed latent contributions, true decoder versus original output writes, exact remainder and fitted intercept. Metadata-picked cases and post-hoc worst failures are labeled separately.','']
 fixedrows=[]
 for m in FEATURES:
  r=next((r for r in fm if r['population']=='primary_ordinary' and r['method']=='native' and r['feature']==str(m)),None)
  if r:fixedrows.append([f'[feature {m}](feature_{m}.md)',r['NMSE_fitvar'],r['active_relative_RMSE'],r['meaningful_activity'],r['well_read']])
 lines += [table(['feature','NMSE_fitvar','active relative RMSE','support','well read'],fixedrows),'', '## 8. What this establishes and what remains unsupported','', 'Readability flags, finite-response compatibility, local derivative agreement, output compatibility and coefficient stability must be read separately. Successful affine prediction supports a candidate realization in these specified transcoder coordinates on the tested population. It does not make M ground truth, identify an original causal pathway, certify independent latent manipulation, or establish compactness. Failed linear correspondence does not rule out nonlinear or other group-level relationships. No rescue model or next experiment was launched.','', '## Execution and reproducibility','', 'Actual commands, tests, stage timings, exit statuses and source snapshots accompany this run. All network and regression/SVD/derivative workloads ran on CUDA; CPU metadata and descriptive aggregation are explicit. Mathematical tests include known mappings, native-copy/permutation/rescaling and perfect-output/unreadable-latent controls. The latter demonstrates why output imitation alone cannot imply latent recovery. Model weights and checkpoint bytes remain fixed.','']
 (run/'SUMMARY.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');plots(run,fm,response)


